NO. 766, Revenue (U.C.III) Department dated 8-5-1984. While granting exemption as per sub-para (i) of para 4 of the said G.O., four conditions were stipulated as per Clauses (a) to (d) under sub-para (i) of para 4 of the said G.O. which are as follows:-
"(a) that it should not be leased out or sold without the permission of the Government;
(b) that the land should be utilized for the purpose for which it is exempted within three years from the date of grant of exemption failing which the exemption granted shall stand cancelled and the said land will be subject to the provisions of the
Urban Land (Ceiling and Regulation) Act, 1976
;
(c) that the land may be mortgaged to any Bank as defined in Clause (iii) of Sub-section (1) of Section 19 including Andhra Pradesh State Financial Corporation for the purpose of raising finances for the industry;
(d) that the land so exempted above would vest in the Government after the expiry of the aforementioned lease period under the provisions of the said Act."
